      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's understandable that the guilt feels overwhelming, making even small breaks feel fraudulent. That feeling of being a machine is a powerful indicator of burnout, suggesting the system is fundamentally broken, not just tired. If the loop feels inescapable, perhaps the focus needs to shift from finding a \"way out\" to finding one tiny, undeniable moment of self-reclamation. Even a single, deliberate act of self-care, however insignificant, is a refusal to let the machine run you completely.",
      "source": "target",
